    test: pin the coverage floors to flags only (BT-85)
    
    A concurrent worker instance re-introduced an undocumented MIN_PACKAGE_COVERAGE
    env override twice (d446cf2, then d1bdcc7 + de81cee) while this tick was
    verifying the row; the async judge caught it and FAILed the row (verdict
    .gitreins/history/2026-11-03/ee1b48e8 -> INCOMPLETE), and the override is out of
    the tree. Nothing ever set that variable: no test, Makefile target, CI step or
    README sentence referenced it, and the README states the floors live in the
    Makefile only and cannot drift — on a coverage gate an env-provided floor is a
    hidden bypass: any shell or job exporting the name changes the verdict with no
    reviewable diff.
    
    This commit keeps the rule enforced instead of trusting a revert:
    TestCovercheckFloorsComeOnlyFromFlags sets MIN_PACKAGE_COVERAGE, MIN_PACKAGE and
    MIN_PACKAGE_FLOOR and asserts the verdict is unchanged, so a future re-add fails
    the suite instead of needing a forensic diff. An intentional floor change must be
    an explicit --min-package flag or a Makefile edit — both reviewable.
    
    ch:trace: row=BT-85 test=TestCovercheckFloorsComeOnlyFromFlags evidence=make cover-check verdict=pending
    
